surface-arclength-gamma-full.out
Material arc length with the full displacement norm, without an hpc mask
StaticStructural solverType "matcalm" loadlevelguess 1.0 nsteps 1 deltat 1.0 stepLength 0.02 Psi 0. MaxIter 30 rtolv 1.e-11 rtolf 1.e-11 manrmsteps 1 nmodules 1
errorcheck
domain 2dPlaneStress
OutputManager tstep_all dofman_all
ndofman 2 nelem 2 ncrosssect 2 nmat 2 nbc 2 nic 0 nltf 1 nset 2
# Both elements share one unit segment. The left end and both transverse dofs are fixed.
# With s = 1 + u_2x, their combined energy is
# W(s,lambda) = 0.5 lambda s - 0.5 s + 0.5 (s^2 - 1) - ln(s).
# Equilibrium therefore gives lambda = 1 - 2 (s - 1/s).
# loadlevelguess 1 starts at the exact equilibrium s=1. With only one free dof, the full displacement norm
# gives |u|=0.02, hence s=0.98 and lambda=1.0808163265306122. No hpc mask is supplied.
# Only element 1 depends on lambda. Element 2 must contribute to the ordinary residual and tangent,
# but its derivative with respect to lambda is zero. Including its stress in the material load vector
# cancels element 1's reference load at s=1 and produces a NaN predictor.
node 1 coords 2 0 0
node 2 coords 2 1 0
lineplanestrainsurface 1 nodes 2 1 2 crosssect 1 nlgeo 1
lineplanestrainsurface 2 nodes 2 1 2 crosssect 2 nlgeo 1
simplesurfacecs 1 material 1
simplesurfacecs 2 material 2
surfacetensionmat 1 gamma1 0.5 d 1 arclenghtpar 1
surfacetensionmat 2 gamma1 -0.5 mu 1 d 1
BoundaryCondition 1 loadTimeFunction 1 dofs 1 1 values 1 0 set 1
BoundaryCondition 2 loadTimeFunction 1 dofs 1 2 values 1 0 set 2
ConstantFunction 1 f(t) 1
Set 1 nodes 1 1
Set 2 nodes 2 1 2
#%BEGIN_CHECK% tolerance 1.e-9
#NODE tStep 1 number 2 dof 1 unknown d value -0.02
#NODE tStep 1 number 2 dof 2 unknown d value 0.0
#LOADLEVEL tStep 1 value 1.0808163265306122
#%END_CHECK%